('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000002',
'Rules',
'Covent Garden',
'Continental',
'Rules opened in 1798, which makes it the oldest restaurant in London and one of the oldest in the world. Thomas Hardy ate here. Charles Dickens ate here. Graham Greene had a regular table. The menu has not substantially changed: game, pies, puddings, claret. The interior — cartoons, paintings, antlers, burgundy banquettes — has not changed either. The experience of eating in a room where significant people have eaten for 226 years is not reproducible elsewhere.',
