'Soho',
'Continental',
'A restored 1930s French brasserie in the basement of what was once the Regent Palace Hotel on Sherwood Street. At under £30 for three courses and a glass of house wine, it offers the best value in central London for a genuinely beautiful room. The ceiling is painted gold, the columns are marble, the portions are Parisian, and the steak frites are correct. No pretension. Remarkable value. A room that has earned its own mythology.',
